    "title": "The Russian actor who went into the army shared his impression of the service",
    "text": "Gleb, who went to the Kalyuzhny army, answered the reporter's question about why every actor had to serve in the army.\nBecause this is the debt of any citizen of the Russian Federation, he said after the premiere of the movie First First on Olympus, at the Moscow cinema in October.\nThe Russian actor also said that the military service for him was a very interesting and inspiring experience that brings new impressions, new acquaintances, clarifying and explaining a lot.\nIn July, Gleb Kalyuzhny was sworn in the Russian armed forces. The actor said he served in the Semenovsky Regiment, and added that all the conditions of the service were satisfied with him.",
